osite of “fast” is…","correct":"slow","answers":["small","sad","slow","heavy"],"explanation":"“slow” is the opposite of “fast”.","concept":"ant-fast","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-06957","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"They ___ happy.","correct":"are","answers":["are","am","be","is"],"explanation":"The plural subject “they” takes “are”.","concept":"grammar-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-06907","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “light” is…","correct":"heavy","answers":["light","young","big","heavy"],"explanation":"“heavy” is the opposite of “light”.","concept":"ant-light","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-06937","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Which word means a place where doctors treat patients?","correct":"hospital","answers":["library","hospital","market","stadium"],"explanation":"The correct word is “hospital”.","concept":"vocab-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07157","topic":"Comprehension","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Read: “Adam found a wallet and gave it to his teacher.”\n\nWhat quality did Adam show?","correct":"Honesty.","answers":["Laziness.","Carelessness.","Honesty.","Anger."],"explanation":"Returning a lost wallet shows honesty.","concept":"comp-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-06996","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Yesterday, Amir ___ football.","correct":"played","answers":["plays","played","playing","play"],"explanation":"“Yesterday” signals past tense, so use “played”.","concept":"tense-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07037","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Now, the children are ___ in the park.","correct":"playing","answers":["playing","played","play","plays"],"explanation":"After “are”, use the -ing form for an action happening now.","concept":"tense-4","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07101","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Choose the correct question.","correct":"Where are you going?","answers":["Where are you going?","Going where you are?","Where you are going.","Where is you going?"],"explanation":"Questions with “you” use “are” before the subject.","concept":"sentence-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07099","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Choose the correct sentence.","correct":"We are going to the market.","answers":["We going are the market.","We are going to the market.","Are we going market the.","We is going market."],"explanation":"This sentence has correct subject-verb agreement and word order.","concept":"sentence-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-06962","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"I have ___ apple.","correct":"an","answers":["the","a","an","some"],"explanation":"Use “an” before a word that begins with a vowel sound.","concept":"grammar-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07050","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The cat is ___ the box.","correct":"in","answers":["from","to","in","with"],"explanation":"“in” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07115","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Choose the sentence with correct punctuation.","correct":"My name is Hana.","answers":["My name is Hana","both","none","My name is Hana."],"explanation":"A sentence starts with a capital letter and ends with punctuation.","concept":"sentence-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07029","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Last night, they ___ a movie.","correct":"watched","answers":["watches","watched","watching","watch"],"explanation":"“Last night” signals past tense.","concept":"tense-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-06914","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Which word means a place where we borrow books?","correct":"library","answers":["clinic","garage","kitchen","library"],"explanation":"The correct word is “library”.","concept":"vocab-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07003","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Every morning, Siti ___ milk.","correct":"drinks","answers":["drinks","drink","drinking","drank"],"explanation":"A repeated daily action uses the simple present: “drinks”.","concept":"tense-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-06991","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"My sister and I ___ pupils.","correct":"are","answers":["was","am","are","is"],"explanation":"A compound plural subject takes “are”.","concept":"grammar-5","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-5-07063","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The ball is ___ the two chairs.","correct":"between","answers":["into","under","from","between"],"explanation":"“between” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-alig